# graph-layout benchmark build artifacts + results (page/ generated)

# Benchmark build output and results.
#
# Wildcards, not one rule per benchmark. The per-directory list this replaced had
# fallen behind: f32-simd-eval/page/index.html was a 200KB+ generated bundle that
# no rule covered and would have been committed. Only generated SUFFIXES inside
# page/ are ignored, so a hand-written asset there still shows up.
benchmarks/*/results/
benchmarks/*/page/index.html
benchmarks/*/page/*.wasm
benchmarks/*/page/benchmark.js
benchmarks/*/page/benchmark.js.map
benchmarks/*/traces/
# Throwaway browser profile directories created per screenshot/serve invocation
# (benchmarks/screenshot-page.ts writes benchmarks/tmp/screenshot-<engine>-<stamp>).
# Not under benchmarks/*/ so the patterns above do not reach it.
benchmarks/tmp/
# Agent and tooling scratch space. AGENTS.md rule 5 sends temporary files here
# rather than into a package directory, so it must never be committed. Belt and
# braces: the video-exporter tests used to create `tmp/video-exporter-tests`
# through a cwd-relative path and were not caught by any ignore rule, which is how
# a stray directory kept reappearing in a clean checkout.
tmp/
# Captured screenshots. Like results/, these are per-run artifacts of a specific
# machine and moment, and a stale one is worse than none: a capture of a
# multi-canvas page can show a blank canvas for reasons that are in the capture
# path rather than the renderer (see screenshot-page.ts KNOWN LIMITATION), so a
# committed image would be read as a defect that does not exist.
benchmarks/*/screenshots/
# markdown-showcase capture artifacts: diffs/ and evidence/ are per-run temp files,
# but baselines/ are committed as the regression gate.
benchmarks/markdown-showcase/diffs/
benchmarks/markdown-showcase/evidence/
